 "notes": [
  "Primary transcription: GOST R 50571.5.52-2011 HTML (identical (IDT) adoption of IEC 60364-5-52:2009), parsed automatically; row lengths and monotonicity checked programmatically.",
  "Cross-check: all A1/A2/B1/B2/C/E cells (Cu 1.5-240, Al 2.5-240) compared with IEC Table C.52.1 as reproduced by Schneider EIG Fig. G21. C.52.1 groups several method/insulation combinations per column, so agreement is approximate (exact or within ~10 %); E-method columns agree exactly. D1, D2, F, G and sizes 300-630 mm2 are single-source (GOST only).",
  "FIX 1: XLPE Cu method E, 3 loaded, 50 mm2: GOST text shows 102 (non-monotonic typo); 192 from EIG C.52.1, which equals B.52.12 column 3 at neighbouring sizes.",
  "FIX 2: PVC Al method C, 3 loaded, 2.5 mm2: GOST text shows 16.5 (same as B1, but C always exceeds B1); 18.5 from EIG C.52.1. Moderate confidence.",
  "NULL: XLPE Cu G_vertical_spaced 300 mm2 - GOST shows 633, below the 240 mm2 value (719); true value not verified.",
  "Aluminium 2.5-10 mm2 have no D2 values in the source tables -> null. Single-core F/G columns start at 25 mm2; E multicore columns stop at 300 mm2 (400-630 null).",
  "Tables B.52.2-B.52.5: circular conductors assumed up to 16 mm2; larger sizes are shaped conductors but values may be applied to circular ones.",
  "B.52.14/B.52.15 factors do not cover solar or infrared radiation; for cables exposed to sun, IEC calls for an individual calculation per IEC 60287 (clause B.52.2.3). Relevant to high-irradiance hill/mountain sites in Nepal.",
  "No altitude correction exists in IEC 60364-5-52 (full-text search of the IDT GOST text found none).",
  "Annex B is informative: manufacturer data or an IEC 60287 calculation may be used instead.",
  "Mineral-insulated tables (B.52.6-B.52.9) and mineral columns of B.52.14 were not transcribed.",
  "The EIG 'Fig. G23' D1/D2 table (e.g. Cu 1.5 mm2 2xXLPE = 26 A) matches neither 2009 B.52.3 D1 (25) nor D2 (27); it cites older numbering ('table B.52-1') and was not used."
